+R34 UFS consumer source note — 2026-11-20
+
+Read-only source inspection; runtime observations belong to main. Only this note
+was written. No device/USB access, builds, tests, or source changes.
+
+Actual build source root S:
+/home/jia/ios-mix1-build/hakios-lithium-ios16
+Repository root R: F:/IOS-MIX1/upstream/hakios-xnu-kernel
+The S files below were read through WSL; line numbers are actual patched-source
+lines, with upstream R equivalents supplied where useful.
+
+Consumer and dispatch:
+- S/userland/root/etc/inject.conf:1 inserts /redwood/lib/libhakios.dylib into
+  backboardd. S/userland/src/inject.c:1191 selects backboardd; :1245 calls
+  input_start(); :1002 creates input_thread, named "redwood input" at :921.
+  R/userland/src/inject.c equivalents:1176,1230,994,913.
+- S/userland/src/inject.c:931 opens HAKIOS_TOUCH_DEVICE O_RDONLY; :959 reads one
+  complete struct hakios_touch. Successful read precedes sample logging at
+  :962-963. R equivalents:923,951,954-955.
+  R/userland/src/hakios.input.h:18 defines /dev/hakios-touch; :20-22 defines
+  DOWN=1, MOVE=2, UP=3; :31-36 defines time/type/finger/x/y.
+- S/drivers/input/hakios.input.c:261-296 is touch_read(): :282 advances the
+  shared queue head, :284 copies the record to userspace. This is the queue
+  filled by hakios_touch_post_batch() at :200-245.
+- S/userland/src/inject.c:985 calls send_touch(); :820-858 constructs the HID
+  hand/finger events, normalizes x/y by 65535 at :831-832, and calls
+  IOHIDVirtualServiceClientDispatchEvent(screen, hand) at :856.
+  R equivalents:977,812-850,823-824,848.
+
+Existing markers and their evidentiary limits:
+- "LITHIUM TOUCH event type=... finger=... x=... y=... total=..."
+  and "LITHIUM TOUCH report ... posted=...": producer queue acceptance only.
+  F:/IOS-MIX1/ports/hakios-lithium/peripherals/touch-live.inc:81-88 increments
+  posted only after the sink succeeds; touch-live-events.h:245 invokes the real
+  hakios_touch_post_batch(). Neither marker proves any userspace read.
+- "hakios: input: touch screen service <pointer>, buttons <pointer>" at S
+  inject.c:953: a non-null screen follows the service-open handshake. See
+  :715-717 for DeviceOpenedByEventSystem=true, :798-815 for creation/waiting,
+  :739 for 'the event server sets "DeviceOpenedByEventSystem" = ...', and :724
+  for "hakios: input: touch detection mode ...". These show HID service setup/
+  property callbacks, not touch-record consumption or per-event delivery.
+- "hakios: input: sample type N finger F at X Y" at S inject.c:963 is the
+  direct existing evidence that backboardd's consumer read a whole queue record.
+  Only the first FOUR records of this thread are logged (:962), including
+  button types 4/5; later silence cannot establish that consumption stopped.
+  Logging occurs before wake handling and digitizer dispatch.
+- "tl: i N posted US read US sent US" at S inject.c:987-988 is conditional on
+  touch_lat=1 (:927). It follows send_touch(), but that function can return
+  early for an invalid finger or an orphan MOVE/UP (:827-828); the Boolean
+  dispatch return declared at :611 is ignored at :856. Thus "sent" is not an
+  acknowledged HID acceptance or SpringBoard delivery. Wake-mode DOWN becomes
+  a lock-button pair and the rest of that stroke is suppressed (:969-983).
+  Frozen UFS cmdline in reports/hakios-ios16-touch-r34-prepared.json:24 has
+  touch_log=1 and applog=1, but no touch_lat=1; do not expect tl: i in this run.
+
+say() writes to stderr (S inject.c:61-73); the actual generated
+S/userland/root/LaunchDaemons/com.apple.backboardd.plist routes stderr to
+/dev/console. Marker capture/retention is still necessary; absence alone is
+not proof of a failed consumer.
+
+Main-reported posted48, touch-screen-service/detection-mode logs, and
+main_queue_enter establish their respective producer/setup/SpringBoard-start
+milestones. Those markers alone do not establish queue reads, complete HID
+acceptance, UIKit/SpringBoard gesture handling, or visible display response.
+The first-four sample lines can establish consumer reads; no unconditional
+per-event successful-dispatch acknowledgment exists in this consumer path.
+Visible tap/swipe/release behavior remains for the user to report during the
+preserved active run. This note adds no new audit, restart, or test requirement.
